  "role": "Director of Creative Services",
  "summary": "Demand-generation and product campaigns for enterprise audiences across digital, event, social, and regional marketing.",
  "overview": "I led creative for DocuSign's demand-generation campaigns, with a scope that expanded to social, events, regional marketing, and corporate communications. The work connected product features with audience-specific stories across digital and physical formats.",
  "projectBrief": {
    "context": "DocuSign was growing its enterprise business and needed campaign creative that could support demand generation, product stories, partnerships, and regional teams.",
    "challenge": "The work had to make digital agreement products useful and relevant to different audiences while staying consistent across channels and markets.",
    "contribution": "I led creative for all demand-generation campaigns and built a seven-person creative function, with responsibility expanding into social, events, EMEA, APAC, and corporate communications.",
    "approach": "I developed campaign frameworks that paired product features with recognizable customer needs, then adapted the work across digital, print, social, event, and partner formats.",
    "outcome": "The role expanded with the business, establishing a broader creative function that supported demand generation and company-wide marketing programs."
  },
